WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 04 · Course 2 · Organise · For entrepreneurs
People, Culture & Volunteers

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Find, support and keep the people your idea needs, from co-founders to volunteers, fairly from the first role.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:29.504
This module helps you plan the people your idea needs, from co-founders to volunteers, and how you will treat them: fair recruitment, clear terms, a good start, regular check-ins, fair pay, a healthy culture and planned exits.

4
00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:30.504
Why people come first

5
00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:36.919
1. Your first people shape your culture more than any written statement of values.

6
00:00:36.919 --> 00:00:43.333
2. Fair terms set before the first role prevent unfair gaps and disputes later.

7
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:50.007
3. Clear agreements between co-founders protect both the idea and the friendship.

8
00:00:50.407 --> 00:01:00.107
What you will work through: 4.1 Workforce planning · 4.2 Recruitment and fair selection · 4.3 Contracts and terms · 4.4 Onboarding · 4.5 Check-ins, performance and development · 4.6 Pay, careers and recognition · 4.7 Culture, wellbeing and inclusion · 4.8 Volunteers and community contributors · 4.9 Offboarding, handover and continuity · 4.10 Recap: People, Culture & Volunteers

9
00:01:00.507 --> 00:01:01.107
By the end you will have

10
00:01:01.107 --> 00:01:07.522
1. A workforce plan matching skills and time to the work, including your own.

11
00:01:07.522 --> 00:01:13.937
2. Fair recruitment steps, written terms and an onboarding plan for every new person.

12
00:01:13.937 --> 00:01:21.722
3. Pay principles, a clear offer for volunteers and a plan for when people leave.

13
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:22.722
Practical tips

14
00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:28.767
1. Start with yourselves: write down what each co-founder brings and can commit.

15
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:34.811
2. Ask someone you might recruit what would make them want to join.

16
00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:42.596
3. Follow how our example bakery plans its trainees, their mentor and its first hires.

17
00:01:43.196 --> 00:01:45.196
You create: Your People Plan: roles, recruitment, terms, onboarding, pay, culture, volunteers and continuity.

18
00:01:45.196 --> 00:01:49.996
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:51.496 --> 00:01:54.596
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
